Z||000002||RZURCTN||10-30-1999||02:03 PM||||you failed to mention what size motor you have.  I know that on the four cyls. it is fairly simple.  disconnect the wires (don't forget to disconnect the negative battery cable first!!) and remove the two bolts from underneath.  you can then work the starter out from the top of the engine.  good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||10-30-1999||08:59 PM||||Sorry, 5-spd-V6.||||reg||1
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||10-30-1999||09:15 PM||||It's not too bad to do. I have to remove mine to replace the oilpan gasket. Just unhooked the wires (espically the battery cable) and undo the 2 bolts (15mm I believe) and notice where the shim points. The hardest part for me was to get the starter back on. It gets heavy after a while||||reg||1
Z||000005||TOM||10-31-1999||01:25 AM||||A bendix is the thing that kicks the started gear out to engage the flywheel. Then the faster speed of the engine after it start kicks the drive back. Its sort of a one way clutch||||reg||1
